{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015k6HgbPywt99MJ7bSFZgDs","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (38.5KB). Full output saved to: /home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/b3f46640-c6ea-4894-9f99-1f4b85951f76/tool-results/bp8bj3xga.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D21 post-run, 2026-10-21)\n\nWhat the lane might ask next vs what we can already answer. Grammar is always `Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`;\nid `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>`; the registry is `lib.meta` (built-ins = verified/speculative, plus\n`lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` speculative modules ranked in `lib/meta/prebuilt/TARGETS.json`). Check what exists with\n`python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print(sorted(k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'))\"`.\n\n**Status:** `seen Dn` = GM-verified that day (built-in, verified tier) · `prebuilt <module>` = speculative extractor\nregistered (gate passed) · `partial` = some sibling fields registered · `gap` = nothing registered (TARGET name given\nwhen one exists but is not built yet).\n**Tools:** (I) = installed (`.venv/bin/python` import or on the `source bin/env.sh` PATH), (M) = missing.\nIn-window extractors may only import the prebuild gate's `ALLOWED_IMPORTS` (`hctf/prebuild.py:112`: stdlib subset +\n`pefile elftools capstone Crypto androguard pyzipper lib`) and may NOT call `open()` -- so Evtx / regipy / olefile /\noletools / dnfile / LnkParse3 / lief / cryptography / asn1crypto / dpkt / PIL / `sqlite3` / `mailbox` / `wave` are\nworker-only (LLM side) until the allowlist is widened. See gaps `gate-allowlist-*`.\n**Likelihood** reasoning: D9-D15 walked Windows binaries/installers/shortcuts/Office (PE -> PE version -> .NET -> MSI\n-> LNK -> OOXML); the next steps are most plausibly other Windows DFIR artifacts and legacy-Office/CFB siblings,\nplus deeper fields of already-seen families (timed kits are cumulative, D15 added cross-file synthesis).\n**D16 turned to e-mail** (`email.message_id` of one `.eml`; flavor \"replies, forwards, duplicates, reconstructed\nmessages ... stable message identities\"). PE stayed three days (D9-11) with a deeper field each day, so D17-D19 most\nplausibly ask deeper `email.*` fields (In-Reply-To / References / attachments / Received / auth) or a sibling mail\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3f46640-c6ea-4894-9f99-1f4b85951f76","uuid":"3c21c5a8-a6cc-47c5-8791-26a63daa6ff7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:10:21.004Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# metadata-forensics — coverage atlas (as of D21 post-run, 2026-10-21)\n\nWhat the lane might ask next vs what we can already answer. Grammar is always `Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`;\nid `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>`; the registry is `lib.meta` (built-ins = verified/speculative, plus\n`lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` speculative modules ranked in `lib/meta/prebuilt/TARGETS.json`). Check what exists with\n`python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print(sorted(k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'))\"`.\n\n**Status:** `seen Dn` = GM-verified that day (built-in, verified tier) · `prebuilt <module>` = speculative extractor\nregistered (gate passed) · `partial` = some sibling fields registered · `gap` = nothing registered (TARGET name given\nwhen one exists but is not built yet).\n**Tools:** (I) = installed (`.venv/bin/python` import or on the `source bin/env.sh` PATH), (M) = missing.\nIn-window extractors may only import the prebuild gate's `ALLOWED_IMPORTS` (`hctf/prebuild.py:112`: stdlib subset +\n`pefile elftools capstone Crypto androguard pyzipper lib`) and may NOT call `open()` -- so Evtx / regipy / olefile /\noletools / dnfile / LnkParse3 / lief / cryptography / asn1crypto / dpkt / PIL / `sqlite3` / `mailbox` / `wave` are\nworker-only (LLM side) until the allowlist is widened. See gaps `gate-allowlist-*`.\n**Likelihood** reasoning: D9-D15 walked Windows binaries/installers/shortcuts/Office (PE -> PE version -> .NET -> MSI\n-> LNK -> OOXML); the next steps are most plausibly other Windows DFIR artifacts and legacy-Office/CFB siblings,\nplus deeper fields of already-seen families (timed kits are cumulative, D15 added cross-file synthesis).\n**D16 turned to e-mail** (`email.message_id` of one `.eml`; flavor \"replies, forwards, duplicates, reconstructed\nmessages ... stable message identities\"). PE stayed three days (D9-11) with a deeper field each day, so D17-D19 most\nplausibly ask deeper `email.*` fields (In-Reply-To / References / attachments / Received / auth) or a sibling mail\ncontainer (MBOX, Outlook MSG), then cross-message threading as a synthesis question. GM fmt word is `email`, not `eml`.\n**D17 jumped to audio instead** (`media.primary_audio_codec_name` of one PCM `.wav` -> `pcm_s16le`; id\n`d17-audio-001-media-...`: family `audio`, fmt `media`, ffprobe vocabulary). Flavor: \"Voice notes have been\ntranscoded, renamed, and embedded in mail. Determine the actual codecs, connect equivalent recordings, and find the\nstream that breaks the sender's story.\" -> D18-D20 most plausibly: the same `media.*` namespace on OTHER containers/\ncodecs (renamed `.wav` that is MP3/Ogg-Opus/M4A/AMR -- \"actual codecs\"), deeper ffprobe stream fields (sample_rate,\nchannels, duration, bit_rate, format_name, stream count), a multi-stream container where one stream disagrees\n(\"stream that breaks the story\": language/creation_time/encoder/codec), audio as a MIME attachment inside `.eml`\n(\"embedded in mail\" -- D16 + D17 combined), and a cross-recording equivalence synthesis (\"connect equivalent\nrecordings\": same INFO title / correlation id / PCM payload / duration). Video `media.*` (h264 etc.) is the next step\nafter that. Email fields remain warm (D16 family carries over in every timed kit).\n**D17 post-run:** every mode asked only `pcm_s16le` (no transcode delivered); the D17-night prebuild covered the audio\nflavor and `media-video-streams`. Lesson: each new family lands under an ABSTRACT fmt word with tool (ffprobe) vocabulary.\n**D18 \"Frame of Reference\" = video** (`media.primary_video_dimensions` of one h264+aac `video-001.mp4` -> `320x180`; id\n`d18-video-001-media-...`: same fmt `media`, family `video`). Prebuilt `media_video.py` answered it in the race probe\n(~5 s). Flavor: \"Clips, previews, and screen recordings have been mixed together. Use stream geometry to identify\noriginals, crops, and the recording that could not have come from the claimed device.\" -- none of it was asked; all\ngeometry sources agreed (stsd = tkhd = SPS, identity matrix, SAR 1:1) in every set. Audio stayed exactly one day deep\n(D17 codec only), so the `media` namespace is moving ONE stream property per day. Next plausible (D19-D21): more ffprobe\ngeometry (`primary_video_codec_name`, rotation/displaymatrix, SAR/DAR, coded vs display size after SPS/clap crop), the\nclaimed DEVICE (QuickTime mdta make/model/software, `©mak/©mod`, Android keys, handler/encoder/compressor name), stills\nasked through `media.*` (\"previews\": ffprobe opens JPEG/PNG as a 1-stream video -- lib answers `none` today!), a\ngeometry synthesis (originals vs crops, aspect groups, the impossible-device file), then a NEW abstract namespace\n(`image.*`, `archive.*`, `log.*`/`event.*`, `disk.*`).\n**D19 \"Little Endian on the Prairie\" = ELF** (`elf.e_machine_u16_hex` of one `collector-001.elf` -> `0x003e`; id\n`d19-elf-001-elf-...`: plain fmt `elf`, family `elf` -- NOT an abstract `binary.*`). Prebuilt `lib.meta` fmt `elf`\nanswered it in the race probe (~13 s). Same x86-64 LSB ELF64 in every mode/set; the timed kit pools it with the D9 Go PE\nand D12 .NET dll. Media stayed exactly ONE field deep per family (audio D17, video D18) and the lane jumped again, so\nmedia is now warm only as carry-over. Flavor: \"Linux binaries from several systems have been pooled with Windows\nexecutables and renamed data. Determine architecture directly from the ELF header and rebuild deployment groups.\" The\npun is EI_DATA byte order. PE stayed THREE days with a deeper header field each day (D9 machine -> D10 entry RVA ->\nD11 version resource), so D20-D22 most plausibly: deeper ELF fields under the same `_uNN_hex`/spec-name grammar\n(e_entry/e_type/EI_CLASS/EI_DATA/EI_OSABI/e_flags, PT_INTERP, build-id, DT_NEEDED/SONAME/RUNPATH, `.comment`,\nNT_GNU_ABI_TAG, section names) on a big-endian or 32-bit ELF (\"several systems\"), a non-ELF renamed `.elf` -> `none`\n(\"renamed data\"), an architecture/deployment-group synthesis across ELF+PE+Mach-O members (\"rebuild deployment\ngroups\"), then Mach-O (fat/thin, LC_UUID, codesign) or Linux packaging (deb/rpm/AppImage) as the next family.\n**D20 \"Universal Appeal\" = Mach-O** (`macho.cpu_type_set` of one `macos-001.bin` -> `[\"0x0100000c\"]`; id\n`d20-macho-001-macho-...`: plain fmt `macho`). ELF stayed ONE day (like audio/video), so the lane is walking executable\nFORMATS one header field each: PE (D9) -> ELF (D19) -> Mach-O (D20). Artifact = a 56-B THIN arm64 header (MH_MAGIC_64\nLE + LC_UUID), identical in every mode/set. GM spelling = raw u32 struct hex inside a JSON list, even without `_hex` in\nthe id; the name `[\"arm64\"]` was REJECTED. First SET-valued header field (one entry per fat slice). Flavor: \"A macOS\ndeployment includes thin and universal binaries mixed with archives. Enumerate every CPU type and identify what truly\nsupports the advertised fleet.\" (fat slices / archives / advertised-vs-actual -- not asked). D21-D23 most plausibly:\n(a) a deeper Mach-O field or a REAL fat binary (cputype set over fat_arch slices, cpusubtype incl. arm64e/x86_64h,\nfat_arch vs slice-header mismatch = \"what truly supports\"); (b) the \"archives\" side -- `ar` static libraries (`.a`,\nuniversal `.a` = fat of ar), macOS installers (xar `.pkg`, `.dmg` koly), zipped `.app` bundles with Info.plist\n(LSMinimumSystemVersion / LSArchitecturePriority = the \"advertised fleet\"); (c) an arch/fleet synthesis across Mach-O +\nELF + PE (which members run on arm64); (d) the next family after the executable trio: Java/JAR/class, WASM, APK/DEX\n(mobile overlap), MSIX/AppX (Windows packaging with ProcessorArchitecture), cpio payloads, firmware.\n**D21 \"Package Deal\" = Android APK** (`apk.package_name` of one `mobile-001.apk` -> `com.huntress.arena.p<8 digits>`; id\n`d21-apk-001-apk-...`: plain fmt `apk`). Option (d) won: after the executable trio the lane moved to a mobile PACKAGE\n(zip + binary-AXML manifest + classes.dex + v1 `META-INF/*.SF/.RSA` + APK Signing Block). Registry MISS (prebuilt had\n`dex`/`jar`/`java`, no `apk` fmt) -> live LLM worker via `aapt dump badging`, ~32 s, first submit; ratchet adds\n`lib/meta/apk.py` (stdlib AXML walk). Same APK in every mode/set; TT 26 / Mastery 130 first try; synthesis now lists\nFIVE files (note/png/dll/eml/apk). Flavor: \"Mobile packages have been mirrored under friendly filenames. Recover\nAndroid package identities, distinguish rebuilds from clones, and expose the borrowed product name.\" -> the unasked\nsiblings are versionCode/versionName (rebuild), signer certificate digest (clone = same package/label, different\nsigner), and `android:label` (the \"product name\", possibly a `@string/` reference resolved through resources.arsc).\nSince D17 EVERY family lasted exactly ONE day, so D22-D24 most plausibly: (a) the mobile sibling -- iOS `.ipa`\n(Info.plist CFBundleIdentifier/ShortVersion/MinimumOSVersion, embedded.mobileprovision TeamIdentifier, main Mach-O),\nor Android App Bundle `.aab` (PROTOBUF manifest, not AXML) / split `.apks`/`.xapk`; (b) a deeper APK field if the lane\nbreaks its one-day pattern (label, signer cert sha256, versionCode, min/target SDK, permissions, native-lib ABI set,\nsignature schemes); (c) \"package\" read as SOFTWARE packages -- NuGet `.nupkg`, Python wheel, npm tarball, Chrome\n`.crx`, VSIX, MSIX (built), deb/rpm (built); (d) a clone/rebuild synthesis across several