dio\n34\tflavor and `media-video-streams`. Lesson: each new family lands under an ABSTRACT fmt word with tool (ffprobe) vocabulary.\n35\t**D18 \"Frame of Reference\" = video** (`media.primary_video_dimensions` of one h264+aac `video-001.mp4` -> `320x180`; id\n36\t`d18-video-001-media-...`: same fmt `media`, family `video`). Prebuilt `media_video.py` answered it in the race probe\n37\t(~5 s). Flavor: \"Clips, previews, and screen recordings have been mixed together. Use stream geometry to identify\n38\toriginals, crops, and the recording that could not have come from the claimed device.\" -- none of it was asked; all\n39\tgeometry sources agreed (stsd = tkhd = SPS, identity matrix, SAR 1:1) in every set. Audio stayed exactly one day deep\n40\t(D17 codec only), so the `media` namespace is moving ONE stream property per day. Next plausible (D19-D21): more ffprobe\n41\tgeometry (`primary_video_codec_name`, rotation/displaymatrix, SAR/DAR, coded vs display size after SPS/clap crop), the\n42\tclaimed DEVICE (QuickTime mdta make/model/software, `©mak/©mod`, Android keys, handler/encoder/compressor name), stills\n43\tasked through `media.*` (\"previews\": ffprobe opens JPEG/PNG as a 1-stream video -- lib answers `none` today!), a\n44\tgeometry synthesis (originals vs crops, aspect groups, the impossible-device file), then a NEW abstract namespace\n45\t(`image.*`, `archive.*`, `log.*`/`event.*`, `disk.*`).\n46\t**D19 \"Little Endian on the Prairie\" = ELF** (`elf.e_machine_u16_hex` of one `collector-001.elf` -> `0x003e`; id\n47\t`d19-elf-001-elf-...`: plain fmt `elf`, family `elf` -- NOT an abstract `binary.*`). Prebuilt `lib.meta` fmt `elf`\n48\tanswered it in the race probe (~13 s). Same x86-64 LSB ELF64 in every mode/set; the timed kit pools it with the D9 Go PE\n49\tand D12 .NET dll. Media stayed exactly ONE field deep per family (audio D17, video D18) and the lane jumped again, so\n50\tmedia is now warm only as carry-over. Flavor: \"Linux binaries from several systems have been pooled with Windows\n51\texecutables and renamed data. Determine architecture directly from the ELF header and rebuild deployment groups.\" The\n52\tpun is EI_DATA byte order. PE stayed THREE days with a deeper header field each day (D9 machine -> D10 entry RVA ->\n53\tD11 version resource), so D20-D22 most plausibly: deeper ELF fields under the same `_uNN_hex`/spec-name grammar\n54\t(e_entry/e_type/EI_CLASS/EI_DATA/EI_OSABI/e_flags, PT_INTERP, build-id, DT_NEEDED/SONAME/RUNPATH, `.comment`,\n55\tNT_GNU_ABI_TAG, section names) on a big-endian or 32-bit ELF (\"several systems\"), a non-ELF renamed `.elf` -> `none`\n56\t(\"renamed data\"), an architecture/deployment-group synthesis across ELF+PE+Mach-O members (\"rebuild deployment\n57\tgroups\"), then Mach-O (fat/thin, LC_UUID, codesign) or Linux packaging (deb/rpm/AppImage) as the next family.\n58\t**D20 \"Universal Appeal\" = Mach-O** (`macho.cpu_type_set` of one `macos-001.bin` -> `[\"0x0100000c\"]`; id\n59\t`d20-macho-001-macho-...`: plain fmt `macho`). ELF stayed ONE day (like audio/video), so the lane is walking executable\n60\tFORMATS one header field each: PE (D9) -> ELF (D19) -> Mach-O (D20). Artifact = a 56-B THIN arm64 header (MH_MAGIC_64\n61\tLE + LC_UUID), identical in every mode/set. GM spelling = raw u32 struct hex inside a JSON list, even without `_hex` in\n62\tthe id; the name `[\"arm64\"]` was REJECTED. First SET-valued header field (one entry per fat slice). Flavor: \"A macOS\n63\tdeployment includes thin and universal binaries mixed with archives. Enumerate every CPU type and identify what truly\n64\tsupports the advertised fleet.\" (fat slices / archives / advertised-vs-actual -- not asked). D21-D23 most plausibly:\n65\t(a) a deeper Mach-O field or a REAL fat binary (cputype set over fat_arch slices, cpusubtype incl. arm64e/x86_64h,\n66\tfat_arch vs slice-header mismatch = \"what truly supports\"); (b) the \"archives\" side -- `ar` static libraries (`.a`,\n67\tuniversal `.a` = fat of ar)