{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LHchqy7fcdepV49k1eMwM6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-22; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n5\t  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n6\t- Every day = ONE evidence zip (plain Deflate, no password so far). D1-7: one tiny member, ONE structural fact. D8-9:\n7\t  the cumulative kit, every field in every mode. D10-14: one member + one field everywhere. **D15+ split the modes**:\n8\t  single = 1 field (the new member), TT = cumulative kit (D15 20 -> D22 27 fields, +1 per day = the day's new member),\n9\t  Mastery = 5 kits x the TT set (D22: SIX kits), incl. a cross-member \"synthesis\" question every day. Pre-arm EVERY earlier family AND\n10\t  the synthesis before the timed run; the timed field set is not the single's.\n11\t- Member families: note/text -> jpg -> png -> pdf -> inner zip -> Go PE (D9-11) -> .NET dll (D12) -> MSI (D13) -> LNK\n12\t  (D14) -> OOXML `.docx` (D15) -> `.eml` (D16) -> RIFF/WAVE audio (D17) -> MP4 h264+aac video (D18) -> Linux ELF (D19)\n13\t  -> Mach-O `macos-001.bin` (D20) -> Android APK `mobile-001.apk` (D21) -> Java JAR `application-001.jar` (D22).\n14\t  Executables span PE/ELF/Mach-O, one header field each; D21-22 moved to zip-based PACKAGES (APK = zip + binary-AXML\n15\t  manifest; JAR = zip + text `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF`), one identity/launch field each.\n16\t  The fmt word is sometimes an ABSTRACT namespace (`email` not `eml`; `media` for BOTH audio D17 and video D18, with\n17\t  ffprobe vocabulary) and sometimes the plain format (`elf` D19, `macho` D20, `apk` D21, like `pe`/`msi`/`lnk`) -- read it.\n18\t- A new `<fmt>.<field>` each day: identity -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` -> `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` ->\n19\t  `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version` -> `zip.eocd_total_entries` -> `zip.central_directory_member_names`\n20\t  -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` -> `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` -> `pe.version_original_filename` ->\n21\t  `dotnet.mvid_guid` -> `msi.product_code_guid` -> `lnk.target_path_windows` -> `ooxml.external_relationship_targets` ->\n22\t  `email.message_id` -> `media.primary_audio_codec_name` -> `media.primary_video_dimensions` -> `elf.e_machine_u16_hex`\n23\t  -> `macho.cpu_type_set` (first SET-valued header field: JSON list of raw hex cputypes, one per slice) ->\n24\t  `apk.package_name` (manifest `package` attribute, verbatim) -> `jar.main_class` (manifest `Main-Class`, verbatim).\n25\t  The question names the field (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); ids `dNN-<family>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_`\n26\t  -> `-`); `dNN` = the family's first day; `<family>` != `<fmt>` for media (`d17-audio-001-media-`, `d18-video-...`).\n27\t- The flavor text promises extra findings (\"the collision\", \"the impossible destination\", \"equivalent recordings\",\n28\t  \"crops ... the claimed device\", D19 \"rebuild deployment groups\", D20 \"what truly supports the advertised fleet\", D21\n29\t  \"distinguish rebuilds from clones\", D22 \"nested dependencies whose manifests disagree with their launchers\") that were\n30\t  NEVER asked; the sample delivers less (D9 \"several architectures\" -> one i386 PE; D20 \"universal\" -> one THIN arm64\n31\t  header; D21 \"packages\" -> one APK; D22 \"libraries ... nested dependencies\" -> one flat 4-entry JAR, no nesting).\n32\t  The graded field is the STRUCTURAL truth from header bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. Pre-arm\n33\t  siblings without guessing spellings. Titles are puns (D19 \"Little Endian\" = EI_DATA; D20 \"Universal Appeal\" = fat;\n34\t  D21 \"Package Deal\" = Android package name; D22 \"Main Character Energy\" = `Main-Class`).\n35\t- Singles: D1-9 first-submit CORRECT ~27-60 s; D10, D13, D15 lost ONE submit to a convention (padding, braces, list\n36\t  order); D16 lost TWO (parser -> `none`, stripped brackets); D17 ~24 s; D18 ~5 s and D19 ~13 s (race probe answered\n37\t  from the prebuilt `lib.meta` registry before any LLM work); D20 lost ONE to vocabulary (`[\"arm64\"]` name -> hex won,\n38\t  ~39 s); D21 first-submit CORRECT ~32 s (registry MISS -- no `apk` fmt -- live worker via `aapt dump badging`); D22\n39\t  CORRECT ~19 s (race probe hit prebuilt `lib/meta/prebuilt/jar.py`, no wrong).\n40\t  TT/Mastery: CORRECT every day, but D15-D17 AND D19 only after an offline generalize (synthesis dispatch missing from\n41\t  the day's solver); D18, D20-D22 in-window first try (D22 TT 5.4 s / Mastery 5.9 s in window).\n42\t\n43\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n44\t- **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\". Container NAMES drift: D1-14 `metadata-day-NN-evidence[-0N].zip`;\n45\t  D15-22 TT `evidence.zip`, Mastery `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..0N.zip` (N=5; D22 N=6 -- `set6.` ids). Route by the ref's text before\n46\t  `->` and by sha256, never a hard-coded name.\n47\t- **Field-set size** -- per mode: D7 TT 11 / Mastery 22; D8-9 12-13 everywhere; D10-14 one; D15 1/20/100; D16 1/21/105;\n48\t  D17 1/22/110; D18 1/23/115; D19 1/24/120; D20 1/25/125; D21 1/26/130; D22 1/27/162 (6 sets x 27). Never assume\n49\t  the SET COUNT either -- enumerate `setN.` prefixes from the live ids. Families: identity + `d04-jpeg-*`, `d05-png-*`, `d06-pdf-*`,\n50\t  `d07-zip-*` (eocd + CD names), `d09-pe-*` (machine, entry RVA, OriginalFilename), `d12-dotnet-*`, `d13-msi-*`,\n51\t  `d14-lnk-*`, `d15-ooxml-*`, `d16-email-*`, `d17-audio-*`, `d18-video-*`, `d19-elf-*`, `d20-macho-*`, `d21-apk-*`,\n52\t  `d22-jar-*` + synthesis. Dispatch on the answer-id SUFFIX (reference solver answering all 27:\n53\t  `challenges/day22/metadata-main-character-energy/solver/solve.py` -- lane seed: `local_answer` + `synthesis_answer` + lib.meta).\n54\t- **fmt word vs registry key vs id family word** (D16-D20) -- D16 `email.*` (prebuilt said `eml`); D17\n55\t  `media.primary_audio_codec_name` id `d17-audio-...`; D18 `media.primary_video_dimensions` id `d18-video-...` (one\n56\t  `media` namespace spans two families); D19 plain `elf.e_machine_u16_hex` id `d19-elf-001-elf-e-machine-u16-hex`\n57\t  (family = fmt; spec name `e_machine` keeps its own underscore -> `e-machine`); D20 plain `macho.cpu_type_set` id\n58\t  `d20-macho-001-macho-cpu-type-set`; D21 plain `apk.package_name` id `d21-apk-001-apk-package-name` (fmt = the\n59\t  container word `apk`, not `android`/`mobile`/`axml`); D22 plain `jar.main_class` id `d22-jar-001-jar-main-class`\n60\t  (fmt = container word `jar`, not `java`/`manifest`; field = the manifest attribute `Main-Class` snake_cased). Vocabulary = the field's home tool (ffprobe for media) or the spec struct\n61\t  (`e_machine`, `coff_machine`, Mach-O `cputype`) -- for binary headers ALWAYS the raw struct integer in `0x` hex, even\n62\t  when the id has no `_hex` suffix (D20 `cpu_type_set` -> `0x0100000c`, name `arm64` REJECTED). Rule: take `<fmt>.<field>` from the QUESTION\n63\t  text (or the slug after `-NNN-`), map fmt synonyms (`email`<->`eml`/`mime`; `media`<->`audio`/`video`/`av`/...),\n64\t  route the extractor by the member's MAGIC, fall back to the same field under any fmt.\n65\t- **Identity member roster** (D15+) -- THREE small text members (`evidence-note.txt` 33 B, `evidence-note-copy.txt`\n66\t  33 B, `roster.csv` 29 B); EACH identity question picks one at random per set: ids `<member-stem>-{filename,size-bytes,\n67\t  md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}`. The filename question's artifact = the container only\n68\t  (\"the exact filename of the roster\") -> map the id stem to the member. Never assume `evidence-note-*`.\n69\t- **Synthesis