{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgHLU8JAwdbLj9xCSaTRp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QwA8ejwN4feKLnVUCtBp9B","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json\np=\"reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"); j=s.index(\"```json\",i)+7; k=s.index(\"```\",j)\ng=json.loads(s[j:k])\ng=[x for x in g if x[\"id\"]!=\"jar-manifest-class-versions\"]\nids={x[\"id\"] for x in g}\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"jar-launchers-nested\",\"concept\":\"Launcher / nested JAR fields promised by the D22 flavor (Spring Boot Start-Class vs launcher Main-Class, nested jars, runnable?)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Extend fmt jar (aliases java_archive, war, ear, spring_boot). Fields: start_class (`Start-Class`), spring_boot_version, spring_boot_classes / spring_boot_lib (attr values `BOOT-INF/classes/`, `BOOT-INF/lib/`), main_class_is_launcher (`true` iff Main-Class matches `org.springframework.boot.loader(.launch)?.(Jar|War|Properties)Launcher` or another known launcher), effective_main_class (Start-Class when the Main-Class is a launcher, else Main-Class), nested_jar_names (JSON, CD order, every member ending `.jar`/`.war` incl. BOOT-INF/lib, WEB-INF/lib, lib/), nested_jar_count, main_class_entry_name (`a/b/C.class` from the dotted name), main_class_entry_present / is_runnable (`true` iff main-section Main-Class present AND its .class entry exists; library jar -> `false`, main_class -> `none`), launcher_agent_class, premain_class, agent_class, add_opens/add_exports (JSON split on spaces), enable_native_access, sealed, per-entry section names (JSON, `Name:` values after the first blank line), duplicate main attributes (Java's Manifest keeps the LAST put; record both first/last), manifest_entry_index (JarInputStream only sees MANIFEST.MF as entry 1 or 2 after `META-INF/`; JarFile uses the CD, case-insensitive fallback) -> jar_input_stream_main_class vs jar_file_main_class. Also resolve 3-deep refs `x.zip -> app.jar -> BOOT-INF/lib/dep.jar` and `!/` URL syntax in lib member resolution, so nested manifests answer jar.* fields. Pure zipfile + manifest parser (72-byte lines, ONE-space continuation, CRLF/LF/CR, case-insensitive names).\"},\n {\"id\":\"java-class-entry\",\"concept\":\"Java class-file depth: this/super class, access flags, main-method presence, module-info ModuleMainClass\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt java (aliases class, jvm; also reachable as jar.main_class_* by resolving the Main-Class entry). Constant-pool walk (tags 1 Utf8 u16-len, 3/4 4 B, 5/6 8 B AND two slots, 7/8/16/19/20 u16, 9/10/11/12/17/18 2xu16, 15 u8+u16; modified-UTF-8). Fields: this_class (dotted), super_class, access_flags_u16_hex, interfaces (JSON), field_count, method_names (JSON in file order), has_main_method (`public static void main([Ljava/lang/String;)V`; flags ACC_PUBLIC|ACC_STATIC), main_method_descriptor, source_file (SourceFile attr), major_version/minor_version, java_version (major-44), inner_classes count, kotlin_metadata_present (`Lkotlin/Metadata;` RuntimeVisibleAnnotations). module-info.class: module_name, module_version, module_main_class (ModuleMainClass attr), requires (JSON). Non-class -> `none`. Stdlib struct only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"prefixed-zip-launchers\",\"concept\":\"Self-executing / prefixed archives where magic @0 is not PK (shebang jar, exe+jar overlay, SFX, zipapp)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt zip (+ jar, pyz, sfx aliases). Locate the LAST valid EOCD from the tail; archive_start = eocd_offset - cd_size - cd_offset (prefix length) ; fields: prefix_length_bytes, prefix_kind (`shebang` if `#!`, `pe` if `MZ`+PE, `elf`, `script`, else `data`), shebang_line (first line, verbatim, no newline), pe_overlay_offset_hex (pefile-free: last section raw end), overlay_magic_hex_8, embedded_archive_format (`zip`/`7z`/`rar`/`cab`), embedded_jar_main_class (reuse jar manifest parse on the shifted zip), zipapp_main_present (`__main__.py`), lfh_offsets_relative (true when CD offsets are relative to the prefix, as `zip -A` fixes). Make every existing zip/jar/apk/ooxml extractor tolerate a prefix (python zipfile already does; the hand EOCD walkers must add archive_start). Routing: if magic @0 is not PK but `PK\\\\x05\\\\x06` occurs in the last 64 KiB+22, treat as zip.\"},\n {\"id\":\"python-pyinstaller-zipapp\",\"concept\":\"Python frozen/runnable packages: PyInstaller CArchive TOC, zipapp .pyz, py2exe/Nuitka markers, pyc versions\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt pyinstaller (aliases pyi, python_frozen) on PE/ELF/Mach-O: find cookie `MEI\\\\x0c\\\\x0b\\\\x0a\\\\x0b\\\\x0e` (last occurrence); 2.1+ cookie = magic 8 B, pkg_len u32 BE, toc_offset u32 BE, toc_len u32 BE, pyvers u32 BE (e.g. 311 -> `3.11`), pylib_name 64 B NUL-padded; pkg_start = cookie_end - pkg_len. TOC entries: entry_len u32, data_off u32, cmprsd_len u32, uncmprsd_len u32, cmpr_flag u8, typecode char, name NUL-padded. Fields: python_version, pylib_name, toc_entry_names (JSON), entry_scripts (typecode `s`, minus pyiboot*/pyi_rth_* -> JSON and `entry_script` = the last non-pyi one), pyz_present, binary_names (typecode `b`). fmt pyz (zipapp): main_present, shebang_line, main_module text first line. Also detect py2exe (`PYTHONSCRIPT` resource) and Nuitka (`KAY` onefile payload / `__nuitka` strings) -> packager_name. Stdlib only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"oci-container-image\",\"concept\":\"Container images: docker-save tarballs and OCI image layouts (Entrypoint/Cmd = where execution begins)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt oci (aliases docker, container, image_tar). tarfile over the member: docker-save has `manifest.json` = [{Config, RepoTags, Layers}] (+ `repositories`); OCI layout has `oci-layout` {imageLayoutVersion}, `index.json` (manifests[].digest/mediaType/annotations `org.opencontainers.image.ref.name`), blobs/sha256/<hex> (manifest -> config digest). Fields from the config JSON: architecture, os, variant, created, config_entrypoint (JSON list), config_cmd (JSON list), config_working_dir, config_user, config_env (JSON), config_labels (JSON object), exposed_ports (JSON sorted), history_created_by (JSON), layer_count, rootfs_diff_ids (JSON), repo_tags (JSON), config_digest (`sha256:<hex>`). Spellings: keep JSON strings verbatim.\"},\n {\"id\":\"electron-asar-npm\",\"concept\":\"Node / Electron runnable packages: app.asar archive header, package.json main/bin/scripts\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt asar (alias electron): Chromium Pickle header = u32 LE 4, u32 header_buf_size, u32 pickle payload size, u32 json_len, JSON header {\\\"files\\\": {name: {files:{...}} | {offset: \\\"<decimal str>\\\", size: n, executable?, unpacked?, integrity{algorithm,hash}}}}; file data base = 8 + header_buf_size. Fields: file_names (JSON, depth-first sorted paths), file_count, unpacked_files (JSON), package_name / package_main / package_version from the inner `package.json`, integrity_algorithm. fmt npm / node (package.json anywhere, incl. `package/package.json` in .tgz): name, version, main, bin (JSON), exports (JSON), scripts_preinstall/install/postinstall, dependencies (JSON). Stdlib struct/json/tarfile.\"},\n {\"id\":\"wasm-start-exports\",\"concept\":\"WebAssembly module depth: start function, exports/imports, name and producers custom sections\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt wasm: `\\\\0asm` + version u32 LE 1; section walk (id u8, size LEB128). Fields: section_ids (JSON in order), start_function_index (section 8; absent -> `none`), export_names (JSON file order) + export_kinds (`func`/`table`/`memory`/`global`), has_wasi_start (`_start` export), import_names (JSON `module.field`), import_modules (JSON sorted unique), function_count (section 3), memory_min_pages/max, custom_section_names (JSON), name_section_module_name (subsection 0), producers_language / producers_processed_by / producers_sdk (JSON `name version`), target_features (JSON). LEB128 unsigned decoder; stdlib only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jar-signing-osgi-maven\",\"concept\":\"JAR provenance: v1 signature signer, signed vs unsigned entries, OSGi bundle headers, WAR/EAR descriptors, Maven coordinates of nested deps\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt jar: signature_files (JSON), signer_cert_sha256 / signer_subject_cn / signer_serial_hex (reuse lib/meta/prebuilt/apk_signing.py v1 PKCS#7 walk), sf_digest_algorithm (`SHA-256-Digest-Manifest` key prefix), unsigned_entries (JSON: CD members with no `Name:` digest section in MANIFEST.MF, excluding META-INF signature files), osgi_bundle_symbolic_name / bundle_version / bundle_activator / export_package (JSON), war_servlet_classes (JSON from WEB-INF/web.xml, ns-agnostic local names), war_welcome_files, ear_modules (JSON from META-INF/application.xml), maven_coordinates (JSON list of `groupId:artifactId:version` from every META-INF/maven/*/*/pom.properties, CD order), maven_group_id/artifact_id/version for a single one. Stdlib zipfile + xml.etree.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dotnet-bundle-clickonce\",\"concept\":\".NET deployment packaging: single-file bundle manifest, runtimeconfig/deps.json, ClickOnce entryPoint\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt dotnet_bundle (aliases singlefile, apphost): find the 32-B bundle marker (dotnet/runtime `bundle_marker` SHA-256 bytes `8b 12 02 b9 6a 61 20 38 72 7b 93 02 14 d7 a0 32 13 f5 b9 e6 ef ae 33 18 ee 3b 2d ce 24 b3 6a ae` -- verify against the runtime source) preceded by a u64 LE header offset; header = major/minor u32, file count i32, bundle id (7-bit-len string), [v2+: deps/runtimeconfig offsets+sizes, flags u64], then entries (offset i64, size i64, [compressed size i64 v6+], type u8, path string). Fields: bundle_version, bundle_id, file_names (JSON), file_count, main_assembly (first type-1 assembly matching the apphost name), runtimeconfig_tfm / framework_name / framework_version (JSON in the bundle or a `*.runtimeconfig.json` member). fmt clickonce (`.application`/`.manifest` XML ns urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1/v2): entry_point_command_file, entry_point_parameters, assembly_identity_name/version/public_key_token/processor_architecture, deployment_provider_codebase.\"},\n]\nfor x in new: assert x[\"id\"] not in ids\n# re-rank: D21 APK p1 items now -> 2; iOS ipa -> 2\nfor x in g:\n    if x[\"id\"] in (\"apk-manifest-siblings\",\"apk-signing-certs\",\"apk-label-resources-arsc\",\"apk-clone-rebuild-synthesis\",\"ios-ipa-identity\"): x[\"priority\"]=2\n    if x[\"id\"]==\"software-packages\":\n        x[\"priority\"]=1\n        x[\"detail\"]+=\" D22 note: wheel `entry_points.txt` console_scripts/gui_scripts (JSON `name=module:func`) and npm `bin`/`main` are the 'where execution begins' fields for these formats -- emit them as entry_points / console_scripts.\"\np1=[x for x in g if x[\"priority\"]==1]\nrest=[x for x in g if x[\"priority\"]!=1]\norder = [new[0],new[1],new[2]] + [x for x in p1 if x[\"id\"]==\"software-packages\"] + [x for x in p1 if x[\"id\"]!=\"software-packages\"] \\\n        + [new[3],new[4],new[5],new[6],new[7]] + [x for x in rest if x[\"priority\"]==2] + [new[8]] + [x for x in rest if x[\"priority\"]!=2]\nassert len(order)==len(g)+len(new)\nbody=\"\\n\"+json.dumps(order,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+\"\\n\"\ns=s[:j]+body+s[k:]\nold_rank=s[s.index(\"Ranking (D21 post-run)\"):s.index(\"```json\",s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"))]\ns=s.replace(old_rank,\"\"\"Ranking (D22 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D23-D25 question (runnable-package / launcher / entry-point siblings of\nD21 APK + D22 JAR: nested/launcher jars, class-file entry, prefixed self-executing archives, software packages) with no\nextractor (or a wrong-answer bug in an existing one), or a harness blocker that silently fails a whole family of\nprebuilds. TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items. The D21 APK items dropped to 2 (APK\nlasted one day like every family since D17).\n\n\"\"\")\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nE\npython3 - <<'E'\nimport json\nt=open(\"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md\").read()\ni=t.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"); j=t.index(\"```json\",i)+7; k=t.index(\"```\",j)\ng=json.loads(t[j:k]); st=json.load(open(\"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/prebuild-state.json\"))\nkeys={\"id\",\"concept\",\"priority\",\"action\",\"detail\"}\nassert all(set(x)==keys for x in g), [x[\"id\"] for x in g if set(x)!=keys]\nassert len({x[\"id\"] for x in g})==len(g)\npend=[x[\"id\"] for x in g if x[\"action\"]==\"prebuild\" and not ((s:=st.get(\"metadata-forensics:\"+x[\"id\"],{})).get(\"ok\") or s.get(\"attempts\",0)>=2)]\nprint(len(g), \"pending prebuild:\", len(pend), pend)\nprint(t[i:j+200])\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":815,"cache_read_input_tokens":132280,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":815},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3f46640-c6ea-4894-9f99-1f4b85951f76","uuid":"ce9db6c3-9aa8-4aac-8b64-dd264c9f1ced","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:15:32.027Z","request_id":"req_011CgHLU7u6ePzBAxnBAUZVC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QwA8ejwN4feKLnVUCtBp9B":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json\np=\"reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index(\"## Readiness gaps\"); j=s.index(\"```json\",i)+7; k=s.index(\"```\",j)\ng=json.loads(s[j:k])\ng=[x for x in g if x[\"id\"]!=\"jar-manifest-class-versions\"]\nids={x[\"id\"] for x in g}\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"jar-launchers-nested\",\"concept\":\"Launcher / nested JAR fields promised by the D22 flavor (Spring Boot Start-Class vs launcher Main-Class, nested jars, runnable?)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Extend fmt jar (aliases java_archive, war, ear, spring_boot). Fields: start_class (`Start-Class`), spring_boot_version, spring_boot_classes / spring_boot_lib (attr values `BOOT-INF/classes/`, `BOOT-INF/lib/`), main_class_is_launcher (`true` iff Main-Class matches `org.springframework.boot.loader(.launch)?.(Jar|War|Properties)Launcher` or another known launcher), effective_main_class (Start-Class when the Main-Class is a launcher, else Main-Class), nested_jar_names (JSON, CD order, every member ending `.jar`/`.war` incl. BOOT-INF/lib, WEB-INF/lib, lib/), nested_jar_count, main_class_entry_name (`a/b/C.class` from the dotted name), main_class_entry_present / is_runnable (`true` iff main-section Main-Class present AND its .class entry exists; library jar -> `false`, main_class -> `none`), launcher_agent_class, premain_class, agent_class, add_opens/add_exports (JSON split on spaces), enable_native_access, sealed, per-entry section names (JSON, `Name:` values after the first blank line), duplicate main attributes (Java's Manifest keeps the LAST put; record both first/last), manifest_entry_index (JarInputStream only sees MANIFEST.MF as entry 1 or 2 after `META-INF/`; JarFile uses the CD, case-insensitive fallback) -> jar_input_stream_main_class vs jar_file_main_class. Also resolve 3-deep refs `x.zip -> app.jar -> BOOT-INF/lib/dep.jar` and `!/` URL syntax in lib member resolution, so nested manifests answer jar.* fields. Pure zipfile + manifest parser (72-byte lines, ONE-space continuation, CRLF/LF/CR, case-insensitive names).\"},\n {\"id\":\"java-class-entry\",\"concept\":\"Java class-file depth: this/super class, access flags, main-method presence, module-info ModuleMainClass\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt java (aliases class, jvm; also reachable as jar.main_class_* by resolving the Main-Class entry). Constant-pool walk (tags 1 Utf8 u16-len, 3/4 4 B, 5/6 8 B AND two slots, 7/8/16/19/20 u16, 9/10/11/12/17/18 2xu16, 15 u8+u16; modified-UTF-8). Fields: this_class (dotted), super_class, access_flags_u16_hex, interfaces (JSON), field_count, method_names (JSON in file order), has_main_method (`public static void main([Ljava/lang/String;)V`; flags ACC_PUBLIC|ACC_STATIC), main_method_descriptor, source_file (SourceFile attr), major_version/minor_version, java_version (major-44), inner_classes count, kotlin_metadata_present (`Lkotlin/Metadata;` RuntimeVisibleAnnotations). module-info.class: module_name, module_version, module_main_class (ModuleMainClass attr), requires (JSON). Non-class -> `none`. Stdlib struct only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"prefixed-zip-launchers\",\"concept\":\"Self-executing / prefixed archives where magic @0 is not PK (shebang jar, exe+jar overlay, SFX, zipapp)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt zip (+ jar, pyz, sfx aliases). Locate the LAST valid EOCD from the tail; archive_start = eocd_offset - cd_size - cd_offset (prefix length) ; fields: prefix_length_bytes, prefix_kind (`shebang` if `#!`, `pe` if `MZ`+PE, `elf`, `script`, else `data`), shebang_line (first line, verbatim, no newline), pe_overlay_offset_hex (pefile-free: last section raw end), overlay_magic_hex_8, embedded_archive_format (`zip`/`7z`/`rar`/`cab`), embedded_jar_main_class (reuse jar manifest parse on the shifted zip), zipapp_main_present (`__main__.py`), lfh_offsets_relative (true when CD offsets are relative to the prefix, as `zip -A` fixes). Make every existing zip/jar/apk/ooxml extractor tolerate a prefix (python zipfile already does; the hand EOCD walkers must add archive_start). Routing: if magic @0 is not PK but `PK\\\\x05\\\\x06` occurs in the last 64 KiB+22, treat as zip.\"},\n {\"id\":\"python-pyinstaller-zipapp\",\"concept\":\"Python frozen/runnable packages: PyInstaller CArchive TOC, zipapp .pyz, py2exe/Nuitka markers, pyc versions\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt pyinstaller (aliases pyi, python_frozen) on PE/ELF/Mach-O: find cookie `MEI\\\\x0c\\\\x0b\\\\x0a\\\\x0b\\\\x0e` (last occurrence); 2.1+ cookie = magic 8 B, pkg_len u32 BE, toc_offset u32 BE, toc_len u32 BE, pyvers u32 BE (e.g. 311 -> `3.11`), pylib_name 64 B NUL-padded; pkg_start = cookie_end - pkg_len. TOC entries: entry_len u32, data_off u32, cmprsd_len u32, uncmprsd_len u32, cmpr_flag u8, typecode char, name NUL-padded. Fields: python_version, pylib_name, toc_entry_names (JSON), entry_scripts (typecode `s`, minus pyiboot*/pyi_rth_* -> JSON and `entry_script` = the last non-pyi one), pyz_present, binary_names (typecode `b`). fmt pyz (zipapp): main_present, shebang_line, main_module text first line. Also detect py2exe (`PYTHONSCRIPT` resource) and Nuitka (`KAY` onefile payload / `__nuitka` strings) -> packager_name. Stdlib only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"oci-container-image\",\"concept\":\"Container images: docker-save tarballs and OCI image layouts (Entrypoint/Cmd = where execution begins)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt oci (aliases docker, container, image_tar). tarfile over the member: docker-save has `manifest.json` = [{Config, RepoTags, Layers}] (+ `repositories`); OCI layout has `oci-layout` {imageLayoutVersion}, `index.json` (manifests[].digest/mediaType/annotations `org.opencontainers.image.ref.name`), blobs/sha256/<hex> (manifest -> config digest). Fields from the config JSON: architecture, os, variant, created, config_entrypoint (JSON list), config_cmd (JSON list), config_working_dir, config_user, config_env (JSON), config_labels (JSON object), exposed_ports (JSON sorted), history_created_by (JSON), layer_count, rootfs_diff_ids (JSON), repo_tags (JSON), config_digest (`sha256:<hex>`). Spellings: keep JSON strings verbatim.\"},\n {\"id\":\"electron-asar-npm\",\"concept\":\"Node / Electron runnable packages: app.asar archive header, package.json main/bin/scripts\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt asar (alias electron): Chromium Pickle header = u32 LE 4, u32 header_buf_size, u32 pickle payload size, u32 json_len, JSON header {\\\"files\\\": {name: {files:{...}} | {offset: \\\"<decimal str>\\\", size: n, executable?, unpacked?, integrity{algorithm,hash}}}}; file data base = 8 + header_buf_size. Fields: file_names (JSON, depth-first sorted paths), file_count, unpacked_files (JSON), package_name / package_main / package_version from the inner `package.json`, integrity_algorithm. fmt npm / node (package.json anywhere, incl. `package/package.json` in .tgz): name, version, main, bin (JSON), exports (JSON), scripts_preinstall/install/postinstall, dependencies (JSON). Stdlib struct/json/tarfile.\"},\n {\"id\":\"wasm-start-exports\",\"concept\":\"WebAssembly module depth: start function, exports/imports, name and producers custom sections\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt wasm: `\\\\0asm` + version u32 LE 1; section walk (id u8, size LEB128). Fields: section_ids (JSON in order), start_function_index (section 8; absent -> `none`), export_names (JSON file order) + export_kinds (`func`/`table`/`memory`/`global`), has_wasi_start (`_start` export), import_names (JSON `module.field`), import_modules (JSON sorted unique), function_count (section 3), memory_min_pages/max, custom_section_names (JSON), name_section_module_name (subsection 0), producers_language / producers_processed_by / producers_sdk (JSON `name version`), target_features (JSON). LEB128 unsigned decoder; stdlib only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jar-signing-osgi-maven\",\"concept\":\"JAR provenance: v1 signature signer, signed vs unsigned entries, OSGi bundle headers, WAR/EAR descriptors, Maven coordinates of nested deps\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt jar: signature_files (JSON), signer_cert_sha256 / signer_subject_cn / signer_serial_hex (reuse lib/meta/prebuilt/apk_signing.py v1 PKCS#7 walk), sf_digest_algorithm (`SHA-256-Digest-Manifest` key prefix), unsigned_entries (JSON: CD members with no `Name:` digest section in MANIFEST.MF, excluding META-INF signature files), osgi_bundle_symbolic_name / bundle_version / bundle_activator / export_package (JSON), war_servlet_classes (JSON from WEB-INF/web.xml, ns-agnostic local names), war_welcome_files, ear_modules (JSON from META-INF/application.xml), maven_coordinates (JSON list of `groupId:artifactId:version` from every META-INF/maven/*/*/pom.properties, CD order), maven_group_id/artifact_id/version for a single one. Stdlib zipfile + xml.etree.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dotnet-bundle-clickonce\",\"concept\":\".NET deployment packaging: single-file bundle manifest, runtimeconfig/deps.json, ClickOnce entryPoint\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt dotnet_bundle (aliases singlefile, apphost): find the 32-B bundle marker (dotnet/runtime `bundle_marker` SHA-256 bytes `8b 12 02 b9 6a 61 20 38 72 7b 93 02 14 d7 a0 32 13 f5 b9 e6 ef ae 33 18 ee 3b 2d ce 24 b3 6a ae` -- verify against the runtime source) preceded by a u64 LE header offset; header = major/minor u32, file count i32, bundle id (7-bit-len string), [v2+: deps/runtimeconfig offsets+sizes, flags u64], then entries (offset i64, size i64, [compressed size i64 v6+], type u8, path string). Fields: bundle_version, bundle_id, file_names (JSON), file_count, main_assembly (first type-1 assembly matching the apphost name), runtimeconfig_tfm / framework_name / framework_version (JSON in the bundle or a `*.runtimeconfig.json` member). fmt clickonce (`.application`/`.manifest` XML ns urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1/v2): entry_point_command_file, entry_point_parameters, assembly_identity_name/version/public_key_token/processor_architecture, deployment_provider_codebase.\"},\n]\nfor x in new: assert x[\"id\"] not in ids\n# re-rank: D21 APK p1 items now -> 2; iOS ipa -> 2\nfor x in g:\n    if x[\"id\"] in (\"apk-manifest-siblings\",\"apk-